Ingestion improvements for retrieval quality (found while debugging the "maintenance" query on PDF page 16 / printed page 13):

DONE (diagrams): diagrams carry their section heading path, nearby FIG label and preceding context
  (src/ingestion/layout.py, see flaws.md "Diagram context"). Requires re-ingestion to take effect.

1. DONE: reading order. Text chunks are now built from DocumentLayout (column-aware order, decoded fonts, no overprint copies or running headers/footers); pypdf text is only a fallback. Requires re-ingestion.
2. Store printed page labels. Add a page_label field to ChunkMetadata/Chroma (PDF page 16 is printed as 13), tell the LLM about it, and let page filters / read_page accept either number. Requires re-ingestion.
3. DONE: section context. Text is split at headings and every text / table / diagram chunk starts with "Section: A > B" (embedded), with the same path in ChunkMetadata.section_headings and Chroma "section_path". Content before the first heading uses the document title (from the filename). Page label part waits on #2. Requires re-ingestion.
4. DONE: garbled diagram captions from font encoding (page 18 "(/(&+($7 ...") are decoded (shift of 29) in captions and page text; captions still unreadable after that are dropped. OCR fallback not implemented.
5. PARTLY DONE: splitting is heading-aware (one section per chunk group), and the default chunk size is now 1000 chars with 100 overlap (was 512/50, which cut procedures mid-sentence). Requires re-ingestion with ENABLE_CHANGE_DETECTION=false. Still to do: re-joining words hyphenated across lines ("op-\neration").
8. DONE: hybrid search. Dense similarity blended with BM25 and exact part-number matching (part_numbers metadata at ingestion), in both the first retrieval and search_documents. See requirements/hybrid_search.md. Requires re-ingestion.
6. DONE: query side reads chunk_type / diagram_path / diagram_kind / section_path. The LLM sees a "section" field per passage, has a read_section tool, neighbors stay within the hit's section, and citations show the section.
7. DONE: requirements/query.md refreshed (sections, read_section, citations, conversation history, web UI, current defaults).
